Z||000014||The Fieromaster||08-16-2001||01:51 AM||||RICE is not meant to offend anyone its to ME a name locked onto a car that has stickers for things it doesnt have... has everything to make it look good but runs like $hit or isnt fast at all.... Or its a car that is for example..<P>A Mitsubishi Eclipse GS hardtop with SPYDER stickers all over it... um NO spyder is a DROP TOP!!  (i have seen this before)<P>ALSO rice is a IDIOT with a Civic 4 door with a Type R sticker... NO NO NO Type R is a HATCHBACK!!!!  Imbosiles!!  Thats rice to me...<P>Rice is NOT.. any average OR fast ass import!<P>Ex.. my Eclipse GSX was not rice!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">       <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">    <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">               <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B>||||reg||11
Z||000015||AusFiero||08-16-2001||03:59 AM||||Hmmm maybe they get offended because they know their cars are riced up. Over here a Fiero is not viewed as any sort of white trash car when I have over $32,000 in it. Now tell me why is it offensive to call this riced up ?  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/riced1_1.jpg"> <BR>I just see what I see and call it what it is.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000016||1FST2M6||08-16-2001||09:05 AM||||Generally, being 'ricey' centers around having a lot of Touring style appearance items without any actual performance modifications, but that's not the whole story. Just adding gargantuan exhaust tips, tall spoilers, multitudinous stickers, ground effects, driving lights, hood pins, huge wheels (and calling them rims), etc. doesn't automatically mean you are 'rice'. Style, after all, is a personal thing. <BR>Rice is more of an attitude problem. Ricers confuse appearance with reality, and convince themselves that a car that looks fast is fast. Talking the talk without enough performance work to walk the walk is what makes someone a true Riceboy or Ricegirl. <P>Why can't people realize it's not a ethnicly related term. Ok, we've all seen farris beuller's day off... "...Motorheads, sluts,  dorks, dweebies..." all the same basic idea. but we don't put an ethnic slant on any of those. Ok from now on I'm not calling it "RICE" anymore.. from now on we should all refer to it as "Cheese" please no one from Wisconsin be offended.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>"ooh look he/she paid extra for Cheese" <P>-----<BR>GEES Aus.. that is Cheesy... 2 nonfunctional wings a heavy Body kit and $10,000 in paint work... uuum ok.. Show cars are ok but this is totally a waste of $. Whats the point of having a car to be a Trailer Queen its entire life?  <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 08-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||DRH||08-16-2001||10:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B><P>"ooh look he/she paid extra for Cheese" <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OK... Now <B>I'm</B> offended.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I'm not sure if it's the term "rice" that bothers countiblis or if it's the mentality to make fun of "them" regardless of the word used. countiblis?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Philphine||08-16-2001||11:01 AM||||except for teasing myself sometimes it's not a term i use. i don't want to be stereotyped, and i try not to do it to others.||||reg||1
