Z||000032||Fformula88||08-16-2001||09:48 PM||||I can see where people may be offended by using the term "ricer"  The term is from Japanese cars reffered to as "rice-burners", because of their country of origin.  It was meant to be offensive.<P>I know the term now has taken on a new context.  Any car on the road that somebody thinks is essentially "all show and no go" gets labeled a "ricer".  I'll admit to using the term a lot too, but as many people here not in an ethnically racial context.<P>As for not taking people to a Fiero meet because they don't like cars with huge fart can exhausts and other visual modifications done without regard to good taste, I think thats kind short sighted.  Just because someone makes some ricer posts on a message board doesn't mean he will be rude or nasty to somebody at a meet in person. <P>Your biggest fear is they will kick beat someone up?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">  Just take 'em all out there and have a good time!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
