Z||000052||Mach10||08-18-2001||04:08 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> <BR>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Most of my friends drive like explorers, mountaineers, impalas, and luxury cars. being like i said 28 years of age and work in a cooperate setting.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Why, you self-righteous little eliteist ****. Are you trying to impress us? What part of this thread had anything to do with your "Corporate setting?" I work in a "corporate setting." How does that make you anymore credible or rigtheous than me? For a self-professed "corporate" you sure do lack a few of the essentials: Common sense, professionalism, and good PR. Are your friend's cars a measure against yourself? Other people? Get off your high-horse. You sit there and call us "prejudice redneck assholes." That's nice. First you take something totally out of context, warp it to fit your argument, and lace it with inflammatory comments. I bet your career will go far in the "corporate setting." Maybe as far as Upper Level Maintenace Supervisor. The guy that hands me TP when the stall's out. Practiced handing out cologne samples? You should. I'll bet you'd look really professional wearing a 3-peice while holding a mop. Almost as professional as you do here. <P>Your "black" friend? Good god, man. I don't have any "Black" friends. Just people. Some of them better tanned than I am. I don't differentiate, but you do. So who's the prejudiced one?<P>Have a SUPER day!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 08-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000053||Cheever3000||08-18-2001||06:04 PM||||I started to type how I thought you guys were needlessly beating up the Count for concerns which are not so outrageous - but then I went back and read the first post again - and there's nothing wrong with white trash trailer park folks!  I have a problem with rednecks, but would not be so presumptuous as to start a topic about it.<P>Count, it seems to me that EVERYBODY uses the term 'ricer', regardless of their race.  I know of no other description to use which would ensure people know what you're talking about ('Cheese'? Give me a break).  Even myself, a white corporate-job male, if I were to rice-out a car, I too would be called a ricer.  You and your friend perhaps just need educated as to what & what not to be sensitive about.  Just because he enters a room where a group is being singled out for ridicule, doesn't mean that group is defined by a specific race and it doesn't mean he's next.  If there were a basis for that, EVERYBODY in the room should have the same fear of being the next target.<P>I'd like to respond to the post above about not having black friends.  Maybe you should ask your friends about that - are you sure they would appreciate you not acknowledging their heritage & ancestry?  When I see someone with another color of skin, I <B>see</B> the color, they're not transparent!  But I give them and their race their due respect.  I expect them to give my Irish heritage the same respect.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000054||Songman||08-18-2001||08:23 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B>I have a problem with rednecks, but would not be so presumptuous as to start a topic about it..</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Gosh Cheev! And I thought you liked me too! And me a self-proclaimed redneck....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>But I use the real definition of redneck and not what city folk have come to call redneck and wrap up everything bad they can think of and hang that label on it...<P>This is not the first reference to people who lives in trailers and acting like they are somehow less than the rest of us. I responded to that same attitude just the other day in another thread. I don't live in a trailer but if I did, by God, I'd be glad to have it. And also as I said in the other thread, people that I have met that live in trailers are generally a lot friendlier and down to earth than people who think their fancy houses make them better than everyone else. I'll take real people every time.. regardless of where they live.<P>As I said before, I have been very fortunate in my life and I am very thankful for that.. but I know that doesn't put me above anyone. There's a lot of people who don't know that. I'd hate to be around when any of them lose their material possessions that make them so high and mighty and see how they cope.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-18-2001).]||||reg||1
